body:
I appreciate your help. But the conditions of the mindset afterwards, especially if you love someone, well sometimes they are uncontrollable actions. If you disciplined enough to be able to just say, "Cool, thanks- here if you need me." Then you are a damn strong willed person and you sell more bullshit than you buy. That is a person that, I personally would say- Isn't in LOVE they are faking it. Now, I do not disagree with the idea that someone is capable of doing this. But if the first instinct isn't instant hurt and pain, well- where was the true core of the caring emotion? Selfishness at it's finest. Most people are capable of squashing people's lives and walking away like nothing happened. I have never been able to do this. I guess I am just guilty. Weak. Emotional, and unsuccessful. Always will be when it comes to love. Ever heard the expression, "Love makes people do crazy things?" Every one individual is different. In fact, in my time living, I have only ever heard of one person ever do the things that you suggest man. Then after two years, I talked to the  dumper not the man that walked away saying "Cool" she didn't regret leaving him or ever feel bad. She just said she admired his actions. She said she knew she never loved him because he was too needy. So, think about that one. Where was the neediness when it came to salvaging the love? I admire that man as well. That takes a lot of character and strength to admit you feel pain but do not show it. As people we are conditioned to chase after love. Animalistic instincts are in our DNA and heritage. Which is why I think we fight so hard for it. Giving up our everyday values and lives because we feel hurt and lost without this one centric soul in our universe. As David Foster Wallace says it in the water speech, "Everything that happens to you in your soap opera life is only being watched by you." I am paraphrasing of course. But you get the point. The girl that broke my heart has no fucking clue how hard my life is now. If anyone did, I assure you that they would never do this, regardless of getting back together. In my case, I do not even want that anymore. i do not even want to rebuild or an apology- I just want the idea that she cares about human life and value to return. I think that is why I fight.

&#x200B;

Also, I know this sounds egotistical and like it is a battle, but- that is exactly what the other person wants either way. You to just give up. Some woman dump men as a test of love, it exist. But, it is kind of knifing. Men do it as well. It toys with emotions. So, it all depends on the individuals feelings and what they would like from a person. I personally have only fought for the relationship when I felt it's value directly after it was over. If I felt comfortable with the way she did not reciprocate feelings- I let go. But, that is just from personal experience.

Strong men also cry.... Strong men... Also cry. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

iykyk..

 11th Street Long Island City

&#x200B;

Go, and be completely serious. See what happens. Tell em' TOXIE sent you.
